// spec: TST-001
//
// ⚠️ A defect is a statement about the INTERPRETER and is never compiled.
//
// ⚠️ Run as an ORDINARY program, not a test run: the file does not parse, so
// there is nothing for --test to collect and the diagnostic is the whole of
// the output either way.
//
// TST-001 accepts either quoted form, so 'test ''X'';' names a test called X.
// Only a String is accepted, and 'X' is a Char [LEX-023] -- so this is not
// recognised as a test declaration at all.  It parses as the identifier 'test'
// followed by a Char, and the diagnostic mentions neither tests nor names.

test 'X';
begin
    AssertTrue (True);
end
